<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells out 3-yr, floater coupon T-notes.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells out 3-yr, floater coupon T-notes.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian Finance Ministry's issue of 3-year, floated coupon T-notes with a par value of 35 billion levs was fully sold at the auction last Friday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issue is offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>The coupon of the issue equals the central bank's main interest rate for the period to maturity and changes every time the rate is changed. The main interest rate is now set at 6.96 percent annually.</p>
<p>The average effective annual yield of the issue is 7.97 percent, Finance Ministry figures showed.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said it had changed the issue number to BG2041097127 from BG2041097028, due to previously made technical mistakes.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	  BG2041097127</p>
<p> Maturity		3 years</p>
<p> Par value	     35 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	  July 11</p>
<p> Issue date	    July 17</p>
<p> Maturity date	 July 13, 2000</p>
<p> Bids received	 54,150 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids   96.28 percent</p>
<p> Bids approved	 35,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg sales price     97.75 percent</p>
<p> Avg effective</p>
<p> annual yield	  7.97 percent</p>
<p> Interest payments   January 15, 1998; July 16, 1999</p>
<p>			   January 14, 1999; July 15, 1999</p>
<p>			   January 13, 2000; July 13, 2000</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
